  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "note_21",
      "text": "WORKFLOW: crepuscular (bimodal) activity. Many species are crepuscular, active around dawn and dusk rather than in one consolidated bout. Two things follow. First, the periodogram shows power at 12 h as well as 24 h; a 12 h component is often bimodality rather than a separate rhythm. Second, and more dangerous, a single circular mean phase is actively misleading here: with two peaks roughly 12 h apart the resultant vector is short and its direction lands BETWEEN them, at the time of day the animal is least active. The Rayleigh output shows this, with a low R. Always look at the distribution before you summarise it with one number.",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 24,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 190
    }
